// The Islamic (Hijri) calendar: twelve lunar months of 29 or 30 days,
// years counted from the Hijra in 622.
//
// Three versions, as ICU has them:
//
// - **civil** (tabular): odd months 30 days, even 29, with the last
//   month's 30th day in 11 years of every 30; the epoch Friday 16 July 622.
// - **tbla**: the same table from the astronomical epoch, Thursday 15 July.
// - **umalqura**: Saudi Arabia's official calendar, set from computed
//   moon sightings and published as a table: the months of 1300 to 1600
//   AH come from ICU's copy of it, and dates outside fall back to civil,
//   as ICU's do.
//
// Neither the purely observational calendar nor regional sightings can be
// computed ahead; these are what software uses.

type HijriDate = {
    year: i64,
    month: i64,
    day: i64,
}

type HijriKind =
    | Civil
    | Tabular
    | UmmAlQura

